    {
      "id": "t8xh9gq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nutrition encompasses sequential biological steps required for growth, energy, and maintenance.",
        "Food is categorized into major nutrients: Carbohydrates, Proteins, Fats, Vitamins, and Minerals.",
        "A balanced diet provides essential nutrients in optimal quantities to prevent health disorders.",
        "Malnutrition leads to specific deficiency states and common nutritional disorders."
      ],
      "id": "bva6rku"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gt96hel",
      "content": "• Nutrition is the process of obtaining food and utilizing it for energy and body functions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "20ripcl",
      "content": "• It includes ingestion, digestion, absorption, assimilation and excretion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dc07o2p",
      "content": "• Good nutrition helps maintain physical and mental health."
    },
    {
      "id": "gukc2aq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Steps in Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "12muicp",
      "content": "• Ingestion – Taking food into the body."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1zk9axy",
      "content": "• Digestion – Breaking down complex food into simple molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5llp4hh",
      "content": "• Absorption – Nutrients enter the bloodstream through the intestine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ab0gsna",
      "content": "• Assimilation – Nutrients used by cells for energy and growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3hmqxk1",
      "content": "• Egestion – Removal of undigested waste."
    },
    {
